  "report": {
    "incident_title": "Intermittent checkout failures, but dashboards are all green",
    "outcome": "conclusive",
    "summary": "The checkout failures are real and server-side, not user-side. Since about 10:15-10:20 UTC, the EBS volume behind node ip-10-0-3-17 (eu-west-1c) has been degraded. The three inventory-svc pods on that node (xk2, p9t, m4c) read their local RocksDB stock cache slowly, with p99 around 4.7s against a 3s checkout timeout. Checkout's reserve calls to those pods time out and checkout returns AVAILABILITY_UNCONFIRMED. The dashboards stay green because the error rate is global (~1.2% vs 0.3% baseline), the average latency is dominated by the 15 healthy pods, and the node's pods still pass readiness. AWS reported degraded performance on the volume at 10:12 UTC. No deploys or config changes explain it.",
    "root_cause": "Degraded EBS volume vol-0ab3f9c1 (eu-west-1c) attached to node ip-10-0-3-17. Disk I/O await rose from about 2ms to about 190ms, causing slow local RocksDB stock reads on inventory-svc pods xk2, p9t and m4c. Those reads exceed checkout-svc's 3000ms reserveInventory timeout, so checkout returns AVAILABILITY_UNCONFIRMED to shoppers. Affected traffic is roughly one-sixth of inventory calls (3 of 18 pods), which is why failures are intermittent and why the global dashboards look normal.",
    "confidence": "high",
